chapter Pattern_Unification

session Nipkow_Grobauer_Pattern in Nipkow_Grobauer_Pattern = HOL +
  description \<open>
    Higher-order pattern unification (Nipkow's algorithm) on de Bruijn
    lambda-terms: termination and correctness (most general unifiers for
    well-typed patterns), following Grobauer's pen-and-paper proofs.
  \<close>
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
    "HOL-Proofs-Lambda"
  theories
    Unif_Termination
    Unif_Correctness
  document_files
    "root.bib"
    "root.tex"

session Pure_Lambda in Pure_Lambda = HOL +
  description \<open>
    The lambda-calculus on the terms of Pure (session Pure_Pattern): beta, eta and alpha,
    well-typed terms in a signature (as Sign.cert_term checks them), confluence of beta-eta on
    well-typed terms modulo alpha, alpha-beta-eta-equivalence, strong normalization, normal
    forms, and substitutions of schematic variables.
  \<close>
  sessions
    Pure_Pattern
    "HOL-Proofs-Lambda"
  theories
    Type_Subst
    Pure_Lambda
    Pure_Typing
    Pure_SN
    Pure_Subst
    Pure_Normal
    Pure_Inversion

