session Pure_Thm_Correctness in Pure_Thm_Correctness = Pure_Unify_Correctness +
  description \<open>
    Soundness, completeness and termination of the formalization of bicompose_aux and
    biresolution of Isabelle/Pure's thm.ML (session Pure_Thm), in the semantics of session
    Pure_Unify_Correctness; the results of biresolution are well-typed again, so that
    biresolution is an operation on an abstract type of theorems. The classic proof terms
    (Proofterm.lift_proof, Proofterm.bicompose_proof) are correct with respect to a declarative
    judgment: composition never warns or raises and yields valid proofs, so that biresolution
    is also an operation on theorems with proofs (theory Thm_Proof). Likewise for the tight
    proofs of ZTerm (ZTerm.lift_proof, ZTerm.bicompose_proof), with an invariant up to renaming
    and instantiation of hidden variables (theories ZTerm_Hidden, ZTerm_Thm_Model).
  \<close>
  sessions
    Pure_Thm
  theories
    Bicompose_Correct
    Bicompose_Fin
    Bicompose_Complete
    Biresolution_Correct
    Thm_Type
    Proof_Subst
